ROLE: TypeScript maintainer of the sk-vision runtime.

CONTEXT: `.skilled/skills/sk-vision/vision-runtime/src/plugin.ts` exports `{ id, server, setup }`. `server` is the OpenCode 1 entry: with `SK_VISION_AUTOINSPECT=1` it registers a `chat.message` hook that calls `AttachmentInjector.handle`. `setup` (built by `createSetup`) is the OpenCode 2 entry and today registers only the `/vision` command and, when the project ships a vision template, one `ctx.session.hook('prompt', ...)` callback. OpenCode 2.0.32's prompt hook passes `{ sessionID, messageID, prompt: { text, files?: [{ uri, name?, ... }] }, delivery }` with `prompt` mutable, and `ctx.session.get({ sessionID })` resolves to a session whose optional `model` is `{ id, providerID }`. `AttachmentInjector.evidenceText(images, guaranteed)` (in `src/opencode/attachments.ts`) returns the evidence string or null.

ACTION: Make OpenCode 2 run the automatic image check through the prompt hook. Edit only `src/plugin.ts`:
1. Add an optional `get?(input: { readonly sessionID: string }): Promise<{ readonly model?: { readonly id: string; readonly providerID: string } }>` to `V2PluginContext.session`.
2. Add to `VisionSetupDeps` an optional `createAutoInspect?: (directory: string) => V2AutoInspect | null`, where `interface V2AutoInspect { evidence(images: readonly FilePart[], guaranteed: boolean): Promise<string | null>; dispose(): Promise<void>; }` (import `FilePart` from `@opencode-ai/sdk`).
3. In `createSetup`'s returned function, call `createAutoInspect?.(ctx.location.directory) ?? null` once. If both the template and the auto-inspect are null, keep today's early return. Otherwise register ONE prompt hook that, inside the existing try/catch: (a) when the template exists and `matchVisionTemplate` matches, runs today's command path and returns; (b) otherwise, when auto-inspect exists, maps `input.prompt.files` to `FilePart`s keeping only `image/*` and `application/pdf` mimes from `promptFileMime` (url: a `file://` uri becomes its path via `fileURLToPath` from `node:url`, any other uri is kept as is), returns when none remain, reads the session model through `ctx.session.get` (any failure or missing `get` means no model), computes `guaranteed` with `isTextOnlyModel({ providerID, modelID: id })` from `./model-modality.js`, and appends a non-null evidence string to `input.prompt.text` joined by a blank line. Disposal also awaits `auto.dispose()`.
4. Add `createDefaultAutoInspect(directory)`: returns null unless `process.env.SK_VISION_AUTOINSPECT === '1'`; otherwise builds a `RuntimeClient` (no `notify`, since OpenCode 2 has no server-side toast), a `PhotonProvider(client, { projectDir: directory })` and an `AttachmentInjector`, and returns `{ evidence: (images, g) => injector.evidenceText(images, g), dispose: () => client.close() }`. Pass it as `createAutoInspect` where `setup` is built at the bottom of the file.
Update the `createSetup` doc comment in one sentence to say the prompt hook also carries automatic image inspection. Keep the file's style; no comments naming specs, phases or ids.

FORMAT: Edit in place, then run from `.skilled/skills/sk-vision/vision-runtime`: `bun test` and `bunx tsc --noEmit`. Report both exit codes and counts, and the changed line ranges. Under 150 words.
